AU–COMESA–IGAD Election Observation Mission to the Uganda Elections 2026

The IGAD Secretariat has deployed its Election Observation Mission to Uganda, joining the Joint AU–COMESA–IGAD Election Observers led by the former President of Nigeria, H.E. Goodluck Jonathan, in Kampala, ahead of the General Elections scheduled for 15 January 2026.

H.E. Goodluck Jonathan will be supported by Shemsudin Ahmed Roble, Member of the COMESA Committee of Elders, and Abebe Muluneh, Director of IGAD Peace and Security Division.

Comprising 84 observers, the Mission will assess the electoral process with a focus on credibility, transparency, and peaceful conduct, in accordance with Uganda’s electoral legal framework, the OAU/AU Declaration on the Principles Governing Democratic Elections, the African Charter on Democracy, Elections and Governance (ACDEG), and the International Declaration of Principles for International Election Observation, among other applicable instruments.

#UgandaElections 

